win32u: Flush a window's surface when another thread releases its DC.

Window surfaces are flushed when a thread goes idle in a message wait.
Drawing into a window from another thread that does not wait for
messages stayed off screen until the window's own thread got a message.
WPF's software renderer presents from its render thread with GetDC,
StretchBlt and ReleaseDC, once per change: the first frame of
Affinity's setup window, drawn after its UI thread had gone idle, never
reached the screen, and the window stayed white until hovered or
refocused. Flush the window's (toplevel's) surface when a DC of a
window of another thread is released; a surface with nothing to flush
returns at once.
---
 dlls/win32u/dce.c            | 10 +++++++++-
 dlls/win32u/win32u_private.h |  1 +
 dlls/win32u/window.c         | 15 +++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 25 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/dce.c b/dlls/win32u/dce.c
index 62989a4..27b4d69 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/dce.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/dce.c
@@ -1407,7 +1407,15 @@ HDC WINAPI NtUserGetDCEx( HWND hwnd, HRGN clip_rgn, DWORD flags )
  */
 INT WINAPI NtUserReleaseDC( HWND hwnd, HDC hdc )
 {
-    return release_dc( hwnd, hdc, FALSE );
+    INT ret = release_dc( hwnd, hdc, FALSE );
+
+    /* Window surfaces are flushed when a thread goes idle in a message wait.
+     * Drawing into a window from another thread, one that does not wait for
+     * messages, stayed off screen until the window's own thread got one: WPF's
+     * software renderer presents from its render thread with GetDC, BitBlt
+     * and ReleaseDC, and Affinity's setup window stayed white until hovered. */
+    if (ret && hwnd && !is_current_thread_window( hwnd )) flush_window_surface( hwnd );
+    return ret;
 }
 
